WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.030
There always seems to be room for a few more
bad guys in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:08.130
and if the MCU's going to introduce a few
more villains next time around, here's how

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.990
they could expand to include some of their
best, and weirdest, comics bad guys in Avengers

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:13.860
4.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.400
One of the most interesting aspects of Infinity
War is that Thanos' infamous snap of the fingers

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.970
straight-up killed people, rather than erasing
them from existence.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.789
That means there are a lot of superheroes
in that world who are dead, and since it stands

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:29.359
to reason that at least a few of them will
make it back to the land of the living, that

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:32.450
means that they've got to be somewhere else
in the meantime.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.090
That opens up the possibility of introducing
Mephisto, the Marvel Universe's most prominent

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.250
take on the devil.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.870
There are even connections that are already
waiting to be explored.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.260
Mephisto's role as a bargainer means that
he could be in the perfect position to trade

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.260
something for the heroes' lives.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.400
We know from Doctor Strange that Tony Stark
staying alive is necessary for the heroes

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.470
to win, so maybe there's something Tony has
that Mephisto wants.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.310
Maybe Captain America is going to strike a
deal to bring back his two best friends.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.900
Or, considering that Mephisto was the one
who drove Nakia to become a supervillain in

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.100
the comics by exploiting her love for T'Challa,
maybe she'll be the one who has to make a

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.020
sacrifice to bring the Black Panther back
from the dead.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.880
There's another fun piece of the finger-snap:
it's not just Earth that's affected.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.920
It's explicitly mentioned several times that
Thanos is killing half the universe, which

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.820
means that all of those spacefaring societies
that we've seen in the Guardians of the Galaxy

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.710
movies have also been hit.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:29.259
That leaves outer space weakened and destabilized
on a cosmic scale, making it the perfect time

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.619
for a galaxy-conquering supervillain to show
up and start destroying things.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:36.490
And there’s no one better than for that
role than Annihilus.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.999
In the comics, he's essentially a sentient
space locust hellbent on devouring everything

00:01:40.999 --> 00:01:43.100
in his path across the galaxy.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.939
Since Thanos has apparently retired to a farm
at the end of Infinity War, temporarily shifting

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:52.069
the focus to a more vicious threat could be
a good way to show how big the stakes have

00:01:52.069 --> 00:01:53.069
gotten.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:57.399
Half the universe dying is bad, but it's better
than the other half being wiped out by a dude

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.300
who calls himself The Living Death.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.259
If the MCU is looking to introduce a villain
that could rival Thanos, then they might decide

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:07.249
to go with one of the greats: Doctor Doom.

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:11.920
Decades of stories where he fights Iron Man,
Doctor Strange, and even Spider-Man have shown

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.340
us that he’s adaptable and powerful enough
to pose a threat to anyone, including Thanos

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.340
himself.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.930
He’s even one of the few villains to team
up with the heroes in the original Infinity

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.250
Gauntlet story, and has had designs on the
stones more than a few times in the years

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.250
since.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.790
Of course, there's an obvious sticking point
here.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:33.180
Despite his career of fighting the whole Marvel
Universe, Doom will always be the arch-nemesis

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.990
of the Fantastic Four, and the film rights
to those characters were held by Fox.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.780
With the news that Disney was buying out Fox
and getting those rights back, however, the

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.430
FF could eventually find a home in the MCU.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.980
It’s pretty much inevitable, although Kevin
Feige has said that there are only "vague

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.130
ideas" about how to bring those characters
into the MCU, and that the next few movies

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.800
(including Avengers 4) were set in stone well
before the buyout.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.980
While it's tempting to focus solely on massive
cosmic threats, there’s plenty of room for

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.040
more minor villains to step into the spotlight
and take advantage of the chaos that results

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.270
from half the population of a planet turning
to dust.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:14.020
Believe it or not, that makes Avengers 4 the
perfect opportunity to introduce the Jackal,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.940
best known as the villain directly responsible
for the infamous Clone Saga.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.630
Peter Parker is one of the characters who
gets dusted by Thanos, meaning that there's

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.770
currently no place for one of Marvel's flagship
characters in the next film.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:31.500
There are ways around that, of course, Homecoming
already hinted at the existence of Miles Morales,

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.640
but they could always decide that a clone
of Peter is a good way to go.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.150
If that seems unlikely, consider this: in
the comics, the Jackal is Miles Warren, who

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:44.040
was one of Peter's college professors before
he got obsessed with cloning Spider-Man and

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.120
Gwen Stacy.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.910
She’s never named in the film, but if you
look at the credits for Homecoming, you’ll

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.990
find that Orange Is the New Black's Selinis
Leyva plays a teacher named Ms. Warren.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:57.040
Maybe it’s a coincidence, but with the MCU,
you never know.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.460
One of the more unexpected moments of Infinity
War involved a reappearance from the Red Skull

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.720
as a cosmic harbinger of doom.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.460
Since he's Captain America's arch-nemesis,
it makes sense that he would somehow find

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:13.540
his way back into action, but now it seems
that Brock Rumlow, a.k.a. Crossbones, is going

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.990
to be back in Avengers 4 in some way, too.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:20.630
At this point, that could mean anything from
a flashback sequence to a scene in the afterlife,

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.350
but it could also mean that we'll be seeing
characters returning from the dead who weren't

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.220
just snapped into dust.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.810
If that's the case, then why stop at Skull
and Bones?

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.980
Why not go all out with the whole dang Skeleton
Crew?

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.889
Admittedly, Mother Night and Minister Blood
aren't exactly going to set the world on fire,

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:41.240
but they're no more or less well-known than
Proxima Midnight and Corvus Glaive, so hey,

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.240
why not?

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.920
Finally, we have the character who is quite
possibly the most Marvel Comics of all the

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.780
Marvel villains: M.O.D.O.K., the Mental Organism
Designed Only for Killing.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:56.340
The MCU has gotten weird enough that we've
seen Eitri the Dwarf, the Grandmaster, and

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.980
a cameo appearance from Beta Ray Bill.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.980
Arnim Zola has been in two movies, and while
he admittedly never appeared in his true comic

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.770
book form as a big robot dude with a TV face
in his chest, Winter Soldier brought him pretty

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:08.970
close.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:13.110
So why not follow up the biggest and most
devastating superhero movie of all time by

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:16.389
throwing in the Mental Organism Designed Only
for Killing?

00:05:16.389 --> 00:05:19.690
He’s not the the giant head in a flying
rocket chair that we want.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.480
He’s the giant head in a flying rocket chair
that we need.

